{
  "status": "confirmed-context-retention-difference",
  "release_acceptance": false,
  "input_sha256": "6b76b99ed74d9bdeb312765d0a13c2222a9e918ba1739185c22d7946eb5744ec",
  "package_sha256": "b1145db9df98f71f650bd5ef68581141021434bea287a0692ad39329f5105734",
  "reviewer": "Codex",
  "deterministic_finding": "Actual native SessionRuntime admits a reduced projection then captures the unreduced history again on next preparation. On the same forty-round fixture this repeats 37 tool-result externalizations, 37 metadata evictions and six round prunes. The pinned TS compiler matches the native compiler results exactly but, when called on its prior projection as the pinned AgentSession does, performs zero further reductions. Native next input is 162,663 estimated tokens; retained working-set input is 15,789.",
  "live_observation": "After task 15, provider cache reuse deteriorates in this native run. Task 20 takes 331.0 s; its four requests report 27,306, 26,623, 25,311 and 33,630 uncached input tokens. The captured backend log reports 93,548.90 ms to prefill 33,630 tokens on the final request. This supports investigating context churn; no same-position TS timing exists yet.",
  "limits": [
    "Core fixture uses volatile immutable artifact callbacks, no model and no durable state writes.",
    "Source inspection establishes different retained working-history behavior; the exact live compiled HTTP prefixes were not captured by this installed CLI, so the causal share of each eviction, working-state update and backend cache policy is not quantified.",
    "The live benchmark has frozen source and binaries. No fix has been applied to its running candidate.",
    "Context retention is separate from the route semantic error. Faster or more stable context does not prove a correct answer."
  ],
  "next_fix_constraints": [
    "Keep a separate canonical compiler working set; never reuse provider-encoded messages or appended request-local state as journal history.",
    "Publish a candidate working set only after current generation admission; a stale or rejected preparation cannot alter future context.",
    "Preserve exact durable originals, access control and artifact rehydration. Refresh source/memory/lease evidence each request.",
    "Carry only acknowledged append suffixes; invalidate on non-prefix branch selection, compaction, reopen or incompatible configuration/evidence changes.",
    "Exercise append/tool-pair/steering/failed-commit/stale-preparation/lease/fork/resume boundaries and matched extended live context before adoption."
  ],
